    "summary": "Frog-shaped bowl, of roughly circular form, made of an unidentified wood. The face is carved three dimensionally, while the feet are carved in low relief along the sides and back of the bowl. There is broad sloping rim, carved with three deep grooves. The carving is simple, but very substantial in feel, the bowl being well hollowed out on the inside, and thoroughly encrusted with a deep patina of grease, particularly on the inside.",
